		<IRequirement type="e">
			<_id type="a">GUID ce84d33a-0faa-4727-8a73-59f03f25be25</_id>
			<_myState type="a">8192</_myState>
			<_name type="a">Recieving signal from RC</_name>
			<_modifiedTimeWeak type="a">6.2.2026::14:49:56</_modifiedTimeWeak>
			<_modifiedTime type="a">6.2.2026::13:10:34</_modifiedTime>
			<_lastID type="a">2</_lastID>
			<_body type="a">{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1250\deff0\deflang1045{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset238{\*\fname Arial;}Arial CE;}}%0D
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\f0\fs20 Receiving signal from RC\par%0D
\par%0D
After receiving the signal, the receiver should:\par%0D
\par%0D
1. Validate the recorded signal according to the\par%0D
   defined requirements.\par%0D
2. If the signal meets the requirements, send it to\par%0D
   the Controller for interpretation.\par%0D
\par%0D
2.1. If the gate was moving at a given moment, it\par%0D
     should be stopped, remembering the direction in\par%0D
     which it was moving.\par%0D
2.2. If the gate was at rest, start the movement in\par%0D
     the opposite direction to the previous one.\par%0D
3. If the signal is incorrect, ignore it.\par%0D
}%0D
</_body>
