		<IRequirement type="e">
			<_id type="a">GUID fb48dd21-f583-4f8a-b81e-96656ad5e66d</_id>
			<_myState type="a">8192</_myState>
			<_name type="a">State indication</_name>
			<_modifiedTimeWeak type="a">6.2.2026::14:49:56</_modifiedTimeWeak>
			<_modifiedTime type="a">6.2.2026::13:13:26</_modifiedTime>
			<_body type="a">{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1250\deff0\deflang1045{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset238{\*\fname Arial;}Arial CE;}}%0D
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\f0\fs20 State indication\par%0D
\par%0D
Optionally, the lamp will be blinking, possibly with\par%0D
different rate in case of opening and closing the gate.\par%0D
}%0D
</_body>
		</IRequirement>
		<IRequirement type="e">
			<_id type="a">GUID c1ec4bbd-fe06-4e4f-802f-2ab3dc7d6caa</_id>
			<_myState type="a">8192</_myState>
			<_name type="a">Stopping</_name>
			<_modifiedTimeWeak type="a">6.2.2026::14:49:56</_modifiedTimeWeak>
			<_modifiedTime type="a">6.2.2026::13:13:50</_modifiedTime>
			<_body type="a">{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1250\deff0\deflang1045{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset238{\*\fname Arial;}Arial CE;}}%0D
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\f0\fs20 Stopping\par%0D
\par%0D
Stopping the gate may result from reaching one of the\par%0D
end positions and the occurrence of a collision.\par%0D
\par%0D
The procedure should in order:\par%0D
\par%0D
1. Switch off the drive.\par%0D
2. Turn off the collision detector.\par%0D
3. Optionally, turn off the signal lamp.\par%0D
}%0D
</_body>
		</IRequirement>
		<IRequirement type="e">
			<_id type="a">GUID 26fd1ffd-6b1d-4320-841c-b61adbc1cf71</_id>
			<_myState type="a">8192</_myState>
			<_name type="a">Testing</_name>
			<_modifiedTimeWeak type="a">6.2.2026::14:49:56</_modifiedTimeWeak>
			<_modifiedTime type="a">6.2.2026::12:13:55</_modifiedTime>
			<_body type="a">{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1250\deff0\deflang1045{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset238{\*\fname Arial;}Arial CE;}}%0D
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\f0\fs20 Testing\par%0D
Testing involves sending the 'is_ok()' message\par%0D
}%0D
</_body>
		</IRequirement>
